+# FUSH ERP Mobile — Phase 14.5.48 Lazy List Key Collision Hotfix
+
+## Objective
+Prevent Compose lazy-list crashes caused by duplicate item keys when multiple independent entity lists share one `LazyColumn`.
+
+## Confirmed root cause
+`ExpenseScreens.kt` emitted expense rows keyed only by `expenseId` and sales-representative contribution rows keyed only by `salesRepId` inside the same `LazyColumn`. Independent database sequences can produce the same numeric value (for example `1` and `1`). Compose requires sibling lazy items to have unique keys; the duplicate is often detected only when scrolling reaches the later item, which explains the app closing near the bottom of the page.
+
+## Fix
+Use namespaced string keys that include the entity/list role, such as `expense-<id>`, `rep-contribution-<id>`, `maintenance-work-order-<id>`, and `production-quality-check-<id>`.
+
+The same preventive namespacing is applied to other multi-list lazy workspaces reviewed in this phase: maintenance, production detail, production report, employee profile tabs, sales-representative profile tabs, governance, risk/internal control, geographic profitability, party voucher/audit list helpers, collection-detail rows without a database ID, and production material-availability rows where the same item could theoretically appear more than once.
+
+## Safety boundary
+UI/Compose identity only. No Room schema/entity/migration, DAO query, accounting posting/reversal, expense calculation, inventory quantity/costing, production/quality calculation, maintenance rule, employee compensation, commission logic, governance/risk rule, geographic profitability formula, authentication, permissions, or other domain/business service is intentionally changed.
+
+## Branch version
+87 / `0.15.4.48-ui-lazy-key-hotfix` for UI branch testing only. Central integration owns the final integrated release version.
